<section class="lf-delpol">
  <div class="lf-delpol-inner">
    <span class="lf-delpol-eyebrow">Delivery Protection</span>
    <h2>Parcels Confirmed as Delivered but Reported as Not Received</h2>
    <p>If your order is recorded as delivered but you cannot locate it, please contact us as soon as possible.</p><p>We will investigate the delivery with the courier and review all available evidence. This may include:</p><ul><li>Tracking and delivery scans</li><li>GPS delivery coordinates</li><li>Delivery photographs</li><li>Signature or recipient information</li><li>The delivery address supplied with the order</li><li>Any nominated neighbour or agreed safe-place instructions</li><li>Information provided by the delivery officer</li></ul><p>Customers may also be asked to check with other members of their household, neighbours, reception areas, building management or any agreed safe place.</p><p>Where the evidence does not establish delivery into the customer&rsquo;s physical possession, or to a person or location authorised by the customer, we will deal with the matter in accordance with the customer&rsquo;s statutory rights. This may include a replacement or refund where appropriate.</p><p>Where our investigation concludes that the parcel was correctly delivered to the customer, a person nominated by the customer or an agreed safe place, we may decline an additional refund or replacement.</p><p>If the customer continues to dispute receipt, they may ask the bank or card provider used for the purchase whether the transaction is eligible for a chargeback or, where applicable, a claim under Section 75 of the Consumer Credit Act 1974. We will provide the bank or card provider with the relevant order and delivery evidence and will cooperate fully with its investigation.</p><p>The bank or card provider will independently assess any payment dispute under the applicable scheme rules. A chargeback is not guaranteed and is separate from the customer&rsquo;s statutory rights and any other legal remedies.</p><p class='note'>Nothing in this policy limits or excludes any rights available to customers under the Consumer Rights Act 2015 or other applicable UK law.</p>
  </div>
</section>
<style>
  .lf-delpol{ background:#fff; padding:10px 20px 64px; }
  .lf-delpol-inner{ max-width:900px; margin:0 auto; background:#f0f7f0; border:1px solid #c4dfc9; border-left:4px solid #2a7a4b; border-radius:14px; padding:34px 36px 30px; font-family:'Lato',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; }
  .lf-delpol-eyebrow{ display:block; font-family:'Lato',sans-serif; font-size:11px; font-weight:800; letter-spacing:.2em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#2a7a4b; margin-bottom:9px; }
  .lf-delpol h2{ font-family:'Playfair Display',Georgia,serif; font-weight:600; font-size:clamp(21px,2.8vw,29px); color:#0b1225; margin:0 0 16px; line-height:1.18; }
  .lf-delpol p{ font-size:14.5px; line-height:1.7; color:#3a3a3a; margin:0 0 13px; }
  .lf-delpol ul{ margin:0 0 15px; padding:0; list-style:none; }
  .lf-delpol li{ position:relative; padding-left:24px; font-size:14.5px; line-height:1.55; color:#3a3a3a; margin-bottom:7px; }
  .lf-delpol li:before{ content:''; position:absolute; left:3px; top:8px; width:7px; height:7px; border-radius:50%; background:#2a7a4b; }
  .lf-delpol .note{ font-size:12.5px; color:#5a5a5a; font-style:italic; border-top:1px solid #c4dfc9; padding-top:14px; margin-top:6px; margin-bottom:0; }
</style>
